// Boot-time applier. No user interface, no registration file: it never appears
// in the menu and is started only from the startup list, or by the application
// with the "soak" argument.
//
// The SECUREID here is the package UID, 0xE0001011, and that is not a
// convenience but the condition for autostart working at all. The installer
// registers the startup entry from a file named after the package UID, and the
// system then launches what that entry names only if the executable carries the
// same identifier as its SID. Both halves were measured on the N95, each by its
// own silent failure; findings 50 has the sequence.
//
// So ocgui.exe is the one that moved. Two executables may not claim one SID -
// the installer refuses the whole package and says only "unable to install"
// (findings 49) - and of the two, only ocboot.exe is constrained in which number
// it may take. ocgui.exe keeps 0xE0001011 as its UID3, so the application in the
// menu is the same application as before; only its SID changed, and nothing
// depends on that since the record moved to a public directory (ocbootcfg.cpp).
//
// UID3 stays 0xE0001013, which is free on both phones. It is not what the
// startup mechanism reads, and two executables in one package sharing a UID3 is
// trouble already paid for once.
//
// Capabilities are the same set as ocgui.exe: the applier opens the same kernel
// channels and would otherwise fail exactly where the application succeeds.

TARGET          ocboot.exe
TARGETTYPE      exe
UID             0 0xE0001013
SECUREID        0xE0001011
VENDORID        0

CAPABILITY      PowerMgmt WriteDeviceData ReadDeviceData ReadUserData WriteUserData ProtServ CommDD

// Same reason as in ocgui.mmp: the relock blob and the clock measurements rely
// on fixed ARM encoding.
ALWAYS_BUILD_AS_ARM

EPOCSTACKSIZE   0x5000
EPOCHEAPSIZE    0x10000 0x800000

SOURCEPATH      ..\src
SOURCE          ocbootmain.cpp
SOURCE          ocbootcfg.cpp
SOURCE          ocengine.cpp
SOURCE          octests.cpp

// Startup list entry. The compiled name does not matter: the package installs
// it into the Startup import directory under the application UID.
START RESOURCE  ocboot_startup.rss
TARGET          ocboot_startup
TARGETPATH      \private\101f875a\import
END

SYSTEMINCLUDE   \epoc32\include

LIBRARY         euser.lib
LIBRARY         efsrv.lib
LIBRARY         hal.lib
LIBRARY         sysutil.lib
